      "threads": [
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "MiCA compliance race",
          "why": "Readers tracked which firms secured licenses, which stablecoins got delisted, and how 27-nation passporting reshapes the competitive map — MiCA as live market-sorting event, not abstract law."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Custodial wallet ban",
          "why": "The EU Parliament committee vote to ban crypto transactions through custodial wallets hit a nerve because it directly threatened how most retail users hold and move crypto."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Stablecoin sovereignty fight",
          "why": "ECB fears of US stablecoins draining EU capital, Tether CEO calling MiCA rules 'very dangerous,' and Kraken reviewing Tether support framed stablecoins as a geopolitical battleground."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "US–EU regulatory competition",
          "why": "Trump tariffs on the EU and the DAMS-vs-MiCA comparison gave readers a horse race framing — which jurisdiction wins crypto firms and sets the global standard."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Self-custody address treatment",
          "why": "The Transfer of Funds Regulation's treatment of self-hosted wallets raised existential questions about whether non-custodial crypto remains viable for EU users."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Licensing arbitrage and passporting",
          "why": "France's pushback on firms licensed in lenient jurisdictions and uneven MiCA enforcement exposed the gap between a single rulebook and 27 different regulators applying it."
        }
      ]
    },
